# Set 2: Technical Errors
2.1:FAT32 not currently supported\n
2.2:Problem printing out defragmentation factors.\n
2.3:Suspicious descriptor in boot\n
2.4:BOOTs are different\n
2.5:Problem reading BOOT(s)\n
2.6:FATs are different\n
2.7:Problem reading FAT(s)\n
2.8:\nProblem scanning surface\n
2.9:Error accessing the volume\n
2.10:\nErrors were found. You did not use the /F switch. Errors are not corrected\n\n

# Set 3: Usage / Status
3.1:Checks a volume and returns a status report\nUsage:\n\tChkdsk [<volume>] [%cf] [%cd <files>] [%cr] [%cs] [%cv]\n\n%cf: attempt to fix any errors found.\n%cd: print out the indicated files and show the fragmentation factor.\n%cr: scan the data area and try to recover unreadable data.\n%cs: only show drive summary.\n%cv: show file name as it is being checked.\n\nNote: if volume is ommited, the current drive is assumed.\n
3.2:Elapsed time: %lds\n

